    "field": "Coastal vulnerability to climate change",
    "problem": "Existing participatory vulnerability assessment tools for coastal communities in the Indo-Pacific either do not fully use accessible scientific information or require technical expertise and data that are not available at the local level, hindering effective, collaborative climate adaptation planning.",
    "method": "The paper presents a participatory vulnerability assessment tool using scoring rubrics to guide non-specialists in rapidly assessing the sensitivity, exposure, and adaptive capacity of tropical coastal communities to climate change impacts.",
    "task": "The task is to present a synoptic, participatory vulnerability assessment tool to help identify the likely impacts of climate change and human activity in tropical coastal areas and facilitate discussions among stakeholders on necessary coping and adaptation measures.",
